IMPORT prelude

-- Societies Act 1966 (Singapore) -- unlawful societies, the offences that go with them, the
-- presumptions that prove them, and the Minister's power to dissolve: ss 14 to 25.
--
-- NAIVE ENCODING. Straight from the deposited text with the writing-l4-rules skill. No pipeline,
-- no coverage table, no independent test pass, no human gate.

§ `Societies Act 1966 -- ss 14 to 25`

§§ `14(1), 9(3), 23(1), 24(3) -- what makes a society unlawful`

-- s 14(1): "Every society, not being a registered society, shall be DEEMED to be an unlawful society; but
-- no society shall be deemed to be unlawful under this section if and so long as the Registrar is
-- satisfied that -- (a) it is organised WHOLLY OUTSIDE SINGAPORE; and (b) does not carry on ANY ACTIVITY
-- in Singapore."
--
-- The default is the offence. A society that is not registered is unlawful, and the only way out of
-- that is the Registrar's satisfaction that it is wholly foreign and wholly inactive here. There are
-- three other routes to the same status: an unapproved branch (s 9(3)), a society that uses a triad
-- ritual, registered or not (s 23(1)), and a society against which a dissolution order has been made
-- (s 24(3)).
DECLARE SocietyStatus HAS
    `is a society within section 2` IS A BOOLEAN
    `is a registered society` IS A BOOLEAN
    `is organised wholly outside Singapore` IS A BOOLEAN
    `carries on any activity in Singapore` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the Registrar is satisfied of both of those things` IS A BOOLEAN
    `is a branch established without the Registrar's prior approval` IS A BOOLEAN
    `uses a triad ritual` IS A BOOLEAN
    `a dissolution order has been made against it under section 24` IS A BOOLEAN

GIVEN `the status` IS A SocietyStatus
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the foreign exemption in section 14(1) applies` IF
        `the status`'s `is organised wholly outside Singapore`
    AND NOT `the status`'s `carries on any activity in Singapore`
    AND `the status`'s `the Registrar is satisfied of both of those things`

GIVEN `the status` IS A SocietyStatus
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the society is an unlawful society` IF
        (    `the status`'s `is a society within section 2`
         AND NOT `the status`'s `is a registered society`
         AND NOT `the foreign exemption in section 14(1) applies` `the status`)
    OR  `the status`'s `is a branch established without the Registrar's prior approval`
    OR  `the status`'s `uses a triad ritual`
    OR  `the status`'s `a dissolution order has been made against it under section 24`

§§ `14 to 20, 23 -- the offences`

-- Each offence and its maximum: a fine and a term of imprisonment, expressed here in months.
--   s 14(2) managing or assisting in the management of an unlawful society: $10,000, 5 years;
--   s 14(3) being or acting as a member of one, or attending a meeting of one: $10,000, 3 years;
--   s 15(1) knowingly allowing a meeting of one in premises you own, occupy or control: $10,000, 3 years;
--   s 16(1) inciting, inducing or inviting another to become a member or help manage one: $10,000, 3 years;
--   s 16(2) violence, threat or intimidation to induce someone to do so: $10,000, 4 years;
--   s 17 procuring or attempting to procure subscription or aid for one: $10,000, 2 years;
--   s 18 printing, publishing, selling, posting or (without lawful authority or excuse) possessing its
--        documents: $10,000, 2 years, with forfeiture;
--   s 20 giving a copy of false rules with intent to mislead or defraud: $10,000, 6 months;
--   s 23(2) possessing the books, writings, banners or insignia of a triad society: $10,000, 3 years.
DECLARE Offence IS ONE OF
    `managing or assisting in the management of an unlawful society`
    `being or acting as a member of an unlawful society, or attending its meeting`
    `knowingly allowing a meeting of an unlawful society on premises`
    `inciting, inducing or inviting someone to join or help manage an unlawful society`
    `using violence, threat or intimidation to induce someone to join or help manage an unlawful society`
    `procuring a subscription or aid for an unlawful society`
    `publishing, or possessing without lawful excuse, an unlawful society's documents`
    `giving a copy of false rules with intent to mislead or defraud`
    `possessing the books or insignia of a triad society`

DECLARE Penalty HAS
    `the maximum fine in dollars` IS A NUMBER
    `the maximum imprisonment in months` IS A NUMBER

GIVEN `the offence` IS AN Offence
GIVETH A Penalty
DECIDE `the penalty for the offence` IS
    CONSIDER `the offence`
    WHEN `managing or assisting in the management of an unlawful society`
        THEN Penalty WITH `the maximum fine in dollars` IS 10000, `the maximum imprisonment in months` IS 60
    WHEN `being or acting as a member of an unlawful society, or attending its meeting`
        THEN Penalty WITH `the maximum fine in dollars` IS 10000, `the maximum imprisonment in months` IS 36
    WHEN `knowingly allowing a meeting of an unlawful society on premises`
        THEN Penalty WITH `the maximum fine in dollars` IS 10000, `the maximum imprisonment in months` IS 36
    WHEN `inciting, inducing or inviting someone to join or help manage an unlawful society`
        THEN Penalty WITH `the maximum fine in dollars` IS 10000, `the maximum imprisonment in months` IS 36
    WHEN `using violence, threat or intimidation to induce someone to join or help manage an unlawful society`
        THEN Penalty WITH `the maximum fine in dollars` IS 10000, `the maximum imprisonment in months` IS 48
    WHEN `procuring a subscription or aid for an unlawful society`
        THEN Penalty WITH `the maximum fine in dollars` IS 10000, `the maximum imprisonment in months` IS 24
    WHEN `publishing, or possessing without lawful excuse, an unlawful society's documents`
        THEN Penalty WITH `the maximum fine in dollars` IS 10000, `the maximum imprisonment in months` IS 24
    WHEN `giving a copy of false rules with intent to mislead or defraud`
        THEN Penalty WITH `the maximum fine in dollars` IS 10000, `the maximum imprisonment in months` IS 6
    WHEN `possessing the books or insignia of a triad society`
        THEN Penalty WITH `the maximum fine in dollars` IS 10000, `the maximum imprisonment in months` IS 36

-- s 14(4), s 15(2), s 23(3): "Every offence under [this subsection] shall be deemed to be a
-- NON-BAILABLE offence and an arrestable case within the meaning of the Criminal Procedure Code 2010."
--
-- Read what is on the list and what is not. The MEMBER's offence (3 years), the OWNER-OF-PREMISES offence
-- (3 years) and the triad POSSESSION offence (3 years) are deemed non-bailable. The MANAGER's offence in
-- s 14(2), the most serious of the group at 5 years, is not named in s 14(4), which refers to
-- subsection (3) only.
GIVEN `the offence` IS AN Offence
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the Act deems the offence non-bailable and an arrestable case` IF
    CONSIDER `the offence`
    WHEN `being or acting as a member of an unlawful society, or attending its meeting` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `knowingly allowing a meeting of an unlawful society on premises` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `possessing the books or insignia of a triad society` THEN TRUE
    OTHERWISE FALSE

DECLARE ConductFacts HAS
    `the society is an unlawful society` IS A BOOLEAN
    `manages or assists in the management` IS A BOOLEAN
    `is or acts as a member` IS A BOOLEAN
    `attends a meeting of the society` IS A BOOLEAN
    `knowingly allows a meeting on premises they own, occupy or control` IS A BOOLEAN
    `incites, induces or invites another to join or help manage` IS A BOOLEAN
    `uses violence, threat or intimidation to induce another to join or help manage` IS A BOOLEAN
    `procures or attempts to procure a subscription or aid` IS A BOOLEAN
    `prints, publishes, displays, sells, exposes for sale or posts its documents` IS A BOOLEAN
    `has its documents in their possession` IS A BOOLEAN
    `has lawful authority or excuse for the possession` IS A BOOLEAN

GIVEN `the conduct` IS A ConductFacts
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the person commits the offence in section 14(2)` IF
        `the conduct`'s `the society is an unlawful society`
    AND `the conduct`'s `manages or assists in the management`

GIVEN `the conduct` IS A ConductFacts
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the person commits the offence in section 14(3)` IF
        `the conduct`'s `the society is an unlawful society`
    AND (    `the conduct`'s `is or acts as a member`
         OR  `the conduct`'s `attends a meeting of the society`)

-- An attendance is enough, with no membership and no knowledge that the society is unlawful stated.
GIVEN `the conduct` IS A ConductFacts
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the person commits the offence in section 15(1)` IF
        `the conduct`'s `the society is an unlawful society`
    AND `the conduct`'s `knowingly allows a meeting on premises they own, occupy or control`

GIVEN `the conduct` IS A ConductFacts
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the person commits an offence in section 16` IF
        `the conduct`'s `the society is an unlawful society`
    AND (    `the conduct`'s `incites, induces or invites another to join or help manage`
         OR  `the conduct`'s `uses violence, threat or intimidation to induce another to join or help manage`)

GIVEN `the conduct` IS A ConductFacts
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the person commits the offence in section 17` IF
        `the conduct`'s `the society is an unlawful society`
    AND `the conduct`'s `procures or attempts to procure a subscription or aid`

-- s 18: "Any person who prints, publishes, displays, sells or exposes for sale, or transmits through the
-- post or who, WITHOUT LAWFUL AUTHORITY OR EXCUSE, has in his possession any placard, newspaper, book,
-- circular, pictorial representation or any other document or writing whatsoever which is issued or
-- appears to be issued by or on behalf of or in the interests of an unlawful society".
--
-- The lawful-excuse qualifier attaches to possession only, on the grammar of the sentence. A person
-- who prints or posts such a document has no excuse written in. The document need only APPEAR to be
-- issued by or in the interests of the society.
GIVEN `the conduct` IS A ConductFacts
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the person commits the offence in section 18` IF
        `the conduct`'s `the society is an unlawful society`
    AND (    `the conduct`'s `prints, publishes, displays, sells, exposes for sale or posts its documents`
         OR  (    `the conduct`'s `has its documents in their possession`
              AND NOT `the conduct`'s `has lawful authority or excuse for the possession`))

§§ `21, 22 -- the presumptions`

-- s 21(1): in any prosecution where "it is proved that a club, company, partnership or association
-- EXISTS -- (a) it shall be presumed, until the contrary is proved, that [it] is a society within the
-- meaning of this Act; (b) it shall not be necessary to prove that the society possesses a name; and (c)
-- it shall be presumed until the contrary is proved that it consists of and has at all material times
-- consisted of 10 OR MORE PERSONS."
-- s 21(2): evidence shall be admitted that any person is REPUTED to be a member, that any announcement
-- has been made that the society has been formed, or that "by repute the society is in existence".
--
-- Two elements of the definition of "society" -- that it has ten or more members, and that it is not
-- one of the excluded kinds -- are presumed against the accused, who must disprove them.
GIVEN `it is proved that a club, company, partnership or association exists` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `it is presumed to be a society consisting of 10 or more persons` IF
    `it is proved that a club, company, partnership or association exists`

GIVEN `it is proved that a club, company, partnership or association exists` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the prosecution must prove the society has a name` IF
    FALSE

-- s 22(1): where "any books, accounts, writings, seals, banners or insignia of or relating to or
-- purporting to relate to any society are found in the possession of any person, it shall be presumed,
-- until the contrary is proved, that that person is a MEMBER of the society, and the society ... in
-- existence".
-- s 22(2): "When any books, accounts, LISTS OF MEMBERS or seals of or relating to any society are found
-- in the possession of any person, it shall be FURTHER presumed ... that that person ASSISTS IN THE
-- MANAGEMENT of the society."
--
-- The presumption of membership (3 years) is drawn from possession of books, accounts, writings, seals,
-- banners or insignia. The presumption of assisting in the management (5 years) is drawn from books,
-- accounts, lists of members or seals. A LIST OF MEMBERS alone raises the second presumption and not
-- the first, although s 22(2) says "further".
DECLARE Possession HAS
    `books` IS A BOOLEAN
    `accounts` IS A BOOLEAN
    `writings` IS A BOOLEAN
    `seals` IS A BOOLEAN
    `banners` IS A BOOLEAN
    `insignia` IS A BOOLEAN
    `lists of members` IS A BOOLEAN

GIVEN `the possession` IS A Possession
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the person is presumed a member under section 22(1)` IF
        `the possession`'s `books`
    OR  `the possession`'s `accounts`
    OR  `the possession`'s `writings`
    OR  `the possession`'s `seals`
    OR  `the possession`'s `banners`
    OR  `the possession`'s `insignia`

GIVEN `the possession` IS A Possession
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the person is presumed to assist in the management under section 22(2)` IF
        `the possession`'s `books`
    OR  `the possession`'s `accounts`
    OR  `the possession`'s `lists of members`
    OR  `the possession`'s `seals`

§§ `23 -- triad rituals`

-- s 23(1): "Every society, WHETHER IT IS REGISTERED OR NOT, which uses a triad ritual shall be deemed to
-- be an unlawful society." A registered society that uses a triad ritual is unlawful while registered.
-- s 23(2): possession of the books, writings, banners or insignia "of or relating to any triad society or
-- branch of a triad society, whether the society or branch is established in Singapore or not": $10,000
-- or 3 years or both.
GIVEN `the society is registered` IS A BOOLEAN, `the society uses a triad ritual` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the society is deemed unlawful by section 23(1)` IF
    `the society uses a triad ritual`

§§ `24 -- dissolution by the Minister`

-- s 24(1): "Whenever it APPEARS TO THE MINISTER that --
--   (a) any registered society is being used for unlawful purposes or for purposes prejudicial to public
--       peace, welfare or good order in Singapore or against Singapore's national security or interest;
--   (b) the registration of any society has been procured by fraud or misrepresentation;
--   (c) any registered society is being used for purposes incompatible with the objects and rules of the
--       society;
--   (d) the rules ... are or have been inadequate for its proper management and control and the society
--       has failed without reasonable cause to amend its rules within 3 months of, and in accordance
--       with, a direction from the Registrar;
--   (e) the rules of a political association do not confine its membership to Singapore citizens, and it
--       has failed without reasonable cause to amend them within 3 months of a direction;
--   (f) a political association has such an affiliation or connection with an organisation outside
--       Singapore as the Registrar considers contrary to national security or interest, and has failed to
--       satisfy the Registrar that it has taken appropriate action to sever it within 3 months of a
--       direction; or
--   (g) any registered society has WILFULLY CONTRAVENED any provision of this Act or of any regulations,
--       OR OF ANY OF THE RULES OF THE SOCIETY,
-- the Minister may order that the society shall be dissolved."
-- s 24(1A): "a certificate issued by the Minister charged with the responsibility for internal security
-- stating that the Minister is satisfied that the society ... is being used for purposes against
-- Singapore's national security or interest is CONCLUSIVE EVIDENCE that the society is being used for
-- such purposes."
-- s 24(6): "The fact that a political association uses a name or symbol which is the same as that of an
-- organisation outside Singapore shall be deemed to be sufficient evidence" of affiliation or connection.
--
-- Limb (g) makes a breach of the society's OWN RULES a ground on which the Minister may dissolve it. The
-- test is what "appears to the Minister", the Act provides no appeal against the order, and a society
-- against which it is made is immediately an unlawful society (s 24(3)).
DECLARE DissolutionGrounds HAS
    `it appears the society is used for unlawful purposes, or purposes prejudicial to public peace, welfare or good order, or against national security or interest` IS A BOOLEAN
    `a certificate of the internal security Minister states the society is used for purposes against national security` IS A BOOLEAN
    `it appears registration was procured by fraud or misrepresentation` IS A BOOLEAN
    `it appears the society is used for purposes incompatible with its objects and rules` IS A BOOLEAN
    `its rules are inadequate and it failed without reasonable cause to amend them within 3 months of a direction` IS A BOOLEAN
    `it is a political association whose rules do not confine membership to citizens and it failed without reasonable cause to amend within 3 months of a direction` IS A BOOLEAN
    `it is a political association with a foreign connection and failed to satisfy the Registrar it severed it within 3 months of a direction` IS A BOOLEAN
    `it appears the society wilfully contravened the Act, the regulations or its own rules` IS A BOOLEAN
    `it is a political association using the same name or symbol as an organisation outside Singapore` IS A BOOLEAN

GIVEN `the grounds` IS A DissolutionGrounds
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the ground in section 24(1)(a) is made out` IF
        `the grounds`'s `it appears the society is used for unlawful purposes, or purposes prejudicial to public peace, welfare or good order, or against national security or interest`
    OR  `the grounds`'s `a certificate of the internal security Minister states the society is used for purposes against national security`

GIVEN `the grounds` IS A DissolutionGrounds
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the Minister may order the society dissolved` IF
        `the ground in section 24(1)(a) is made out` `the grounds`
    OR  `the grounds`'s `it appears registration was procured by fraud or misrepresentation`
    OR  `the grounds`'s `it appears the society is used for purposes incompatible with its objects and rules`
    OR  `the grounds`'s `its rules are inadequate and it failed without reasonable cause to amend them within 3 months of a direction`
    OR  `the grounds`'s `it is a political association whose rules do not confine membership to citizens and it failed without reasonable cause to amend within 3 months of a direction`
    OR  `the grounds`'s `it is a political association with a foreign connection and failed to satisfy the Registrar it severed it within 3 months of a direction`
    OR  `the grounds`'s `it appears the society wilfully contravened the Act, the regulations or its own rules`

-- s 24(6): the same name or symbol is deemed sufficient evidence of the foreign connection that limb (f)
-- needs, however the name came to be shared.
GIVEN `the grounds` IS A DissolutionGrounds
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the foreign connection in limb (f) is established by the name or symbol alone` IF
    `the grounds`'s `it is a political association using the same name or symbol as an organisation outside Singapore`

GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the Act provides an appeal or review against an order under section 24` IF
    FALSE

-- s 24(4): every person who was an officer of the society on the date of the order is, for 3 YEARS from
-- that date, "ineligible, except with the written permission of the Minister, to act or be elected as an
-- officer of any other society".
-- s 24(5): acting while ineligible: $10,000 or 2 years or both.
DECLARE IneligibilityFacts HAS
    `was an officer of the society on the date of the dissolution order` IS A BOOLEAN
    `years since the order` IS A NUMBER
    `the Minister gave written permission` IS A BOOLEAN
    `is acting or elected as an officer of another society` IS A BOOLEAN

GIVEN `the person` IS AN IneligibilityFacts
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the person is ineligible under section 24(4)` IF
        `the person`'s `was an officer of the society on the date of the dissolution order`
    AND `the person`'s `years since the order` LESS THAN 3

GIVEN `the person` IS AN IneligibilityFacts
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the person commits the offence in section 24(5)` IF
        `the person is ineligible under section 24(4)` `the person`
    AND NOT `the person`'s `the Minister gave written permission`
    AND `the person`'s `is acting or elected as an officer of another society`

§§ `25 -- what happens to the property`

-- s 25(1): on a dissolution order, "(a) the property of the society shall FORTHWITH VEST either in the
-- Official Receiver or, if any other officer is appointed for the purpose of winding up by the Minister
-- in the notification of the order, then in that officer; and (b) [he] shall proceed to wind up ... and,
-- after satisfying and providing for all debts and liabilities ... and the costs of winding up, shall pay
-- the SURPLUS ASSETS, if any, of the society -- (i) where the Minister so directs, INTO THE CONSOLIDATED
-- FUND; and (ii) in the absence of a direction by the Minister, to the members of the society according to
-- the rules of the society."
-- s 25(3): the Minister may suspend the operation of the section for a period "for the purpose of enabling
-- a society to wind up its own affairs".
--
-- The members' surplus is the default and the Consolidated Fund the Minister's choice: the order decides
-- where the society's money goes, not the society's rules.
GIVEN `the Minister has directed the surplus into the Consolidated Fund` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the surplus goes to the Consolidated Fund` IF
    `the Minister has directed the surplus into the Consolidated Fund`

GIVEN `the Minister has directed the surplus into the Consolidated Fund` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the surplus goes to the members according to the rules` IF
    NOT `the Minister has directed the surplus into the Consolidated Fund`

GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the society's property vests in the Official Receiver or the appointed officer only after a court order` IF
    FALSE
